    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated offensive approach, centered on the dynamic speed profile of **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who clocks in as our highest-rated starter at 80.98. His matchup against Lowder provides the day\u2019s most favorable SP context (+19% skill adjustment), and with wind blowing out, he is primed to capitalize on his platoon advantage to bolster our SB and R totals. **Junior Caminero** (69.27) and **Trea Turner** (67.25) anchor the top of our lineup, with **Trea Turner** specifically benefiting from a +4% SB boost due to Ginn's slow delivery to the plate. While **Kyle Schwarber** (62.65) offers high-floor power from the #2 hole, we are monitoring his performance against Ginn closely to ensure his xwOBA carries over into production.\n\nThe optimization logic for today heavily penalized **Caleb Durbin** (41.71), whose utility is severely hampered by a #9 batting order slot. Despite the strong SB potential against a pitcher with a slow delivery, the -8% order penalty keeps him on the periphery of our daily cap management. The bench decisions today were largely dictated by schedule availability, with **Yordan Alvarez**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** all sidelined by team off-days. **Christian Yelich** remains on the IL, leaving no high-upside alternatives to challenge our current starters. We are currently playing without the depth of **Colt Keith**, **Carson Benge**, or **Gary Sanchez**, forcing us to lean heavily on the top-tier efficiency of our active core. Owners should track the status of **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** as potential late-entry pivots if inclement weather shifts in the afternoon, but for now, the 5x5 Roto strategy remains focused on maximizing the stolen base potential provided by the **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** tandem.",
